From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 182] panvk: optional dump of tiler heap descriptor state
Generated-by: LLM

Debug only: with PANVK_HEAP_TRACE=1, every 64 fragment submissions log
the completed top/bottom range stored by the command stream at fragment
finish, the whole tiler context and the active TILER_HEAP descriptor, to check whether the hardware
reports the chunk range that fragment finish should release. biblioklept

The dump now waits for all iteration scoreboards first, so it cannot race the
tiler write-back (biblioklept).

It also copies the firmware heap context (free list head and counters) at
each fragment CALL and prints the whole 64-byte descriptor slot.

Also dumped: the tiler context as the vertex-tiler side sees it after
FINISH_TILING, the tiler context address on both sides, and the completed
range read right after tiling, before the fragment job runs. Each recorded
render pass logs its tiler context address. PANVK_HEAP_VT_COPY=1 is an
experiment: the VT side copies the completed range to tiler context words
16-19 after tiling and FINISH_FRAGMENT takes it from there. PANVK_HEAP_FF
bits try FINISH_FRAGMENT variants: 1 swaps the chunk arguments, 2 adds
FRAGMENT_END, 4 runs it immediately, 8 waits for the fragment job first,
16 waits for tiling on the VT side. PANVK_KBASE_HEAP_TARGET_IN_FLIGHT sets
the kbase target_in_flight (65535 by default): kbase only grants a new
chunk while that many render passes or fewer are in flight, otherwise the
firmware waits for FINISH_FRAGMENT to return chunks (r44p1 handle_oom_event).
PANVK_KBASE_HEAP_SET_ONCE=1 keeps only the init stream HEAP_SET, as upstream
does, instead of one per CALL. PANVK_KBASE_HEAP_ADAPT=1 sizes the background
spare heap from the tiler work per submission of the retiring heap
(PANVK_KBASE_HEAP_ADAPT_WPS threshold, PANVK_KBASE_HEAP_ADAPT_CHUNKS size)
and skips a renewal instead of waiting when the spare is not ready yet.
The tiler OOM handler keeps a running count of incremental-rendering
passes, logged every 64 fragment jobs with PANVK_IR_STATS=1.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/181

